th the number of installs? Create a binned analysis.**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# average rating for each install range (bins made in the cleaning step)\nrating_by_installs = df.groupby(\"Installs_Bucket\", observed=True)[\"Rating\"].agg([\"mean\", \"count\"]).round(2)\nprint(rating_by_installs)\n\nplt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))\nsns.barplot(x=rating_by_installs.index, y=rating_by_installs[\"mean\"])\nplt.xlabel(\"Install Range\")\nplt.ylabel(\"Average Rating\")\nplt.title(\"Average Rating by Install Range\")\nplt.ylim(3.5, 4.5)\nplt.tight_layout()\nsavefig(\"a3_rating_by_install_range.png\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-12T19:37:29.513339Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-12T19:37:29.51364Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-12T19:37:29.831366Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-12T19:37:29.513615Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-12T19:37:29.830612Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"                 mean  count\nInstalls_Bucket             \n0-1K              4.2   1337\n1K-10K           4.03   1415\n10K-100K         4.09   1572\n100K-1M          4.21   2002\n1M-10M           4.29   1815\n10M-100M         4.38    641\n100M+            4.31    110\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1100x550 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"name":"stdout","text":"Chart saved to: /kaggle/working/images/a3_rating_by_install_range.png\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":77},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"*Average rating goes up as apps get more installs. It is lowest for apps with 1K to 10K installs (4.03) and highest for 10M to 100M installs (4.38). Apps with 100M+ installs stay high at 4.31. Apps with under 1K installs also show a high 4.20, because a few reviews from friends or early users can easily give them a good score. Overall, popular apps usually have better ratings, but the change is small (about 0.35 points), so ratings depend on more than installs.*","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**4. Perform sentiment analysis on app reviews (if review text is available) to determine the common themes in high and low-rated apps.**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# use the cleaned reviews from cell 2 and add each app's rating\nreviews_rated = reviews.copy()\nreviews_rated[\"App_Rating\"] = reviews_rated[\"App\"].map(app_level.set_index(\"App\")[\"Rating\"])\nreviews_rated = reviews_rated.dropna(subset=[\"App_Rating\"])\n\nhigh = reviews_rated[reviews_rated[\"App_Rating\"] >= 4.5]\nlow = reviews_rated[reviews_rated[\"App_Rating\"] < 4.0]\n\nprint(\"High rated apps:\", high[\"App\"].nunique(), \"apps,\", len(high), \"reviews\")\nprint(\"Low rated apps:\", low[\"App\"].nunique(), \"apps,\", len(low), \"reviews\")\n\n# sentiment share in each group\nsentiment = pd.DataFrame({\n    \"High Rated (4.5+)\": high[\"Sentiment\"].value_counts(normalize=True) * 100,\n    \"Low Rated (below 4.0)\": low[\"Sentiment\"].value_counts(normalize=True) * 100\n}).round(1)\nprint(sentiment)\n\nsentiment.plot(kind=\"bar\", figsize=(9, 5))\nplt.xlabel(\"Sentiment\")\nplt.ylabel(\"Percent of Reviews\")\nplt.title(\"Review Sentiment: High vs Low Rated Apps\")\nplt.xticks(rotation=0)\nplt.tight_layout()\nsavefig(\"a4_sentiment_comparison.png\")\n\n# group review words into themes\nthemes = {\n    \"Ease of use\": r\"\\b(?:easy|simple|useful|helpful)\",\n    \"Bugs and crashes\": r\"\\b(?:crash|bug|freeze|error|glitch|fix|stuck)\",\n    \"Updates\": r\"\\b(?:update|version)\",\n    \"Price and payment\": r\"\\b(?:money|price|pay|paid|refund|subscription|purchase)\",\n    \"Login and account\": r\"\\b(?:login|account|password|sign)\",\n    \"Ads\": r\"\\b(?:ads|advert)\",\n    \"Speed\": r\"\\b(?:slow|fast|lag|loading)\"\n}\n\npositive_high = high[high[\"Sentiment\"] == \"Positive\"][\"Translated_Review\"].str.lower()\nnegative_low = low[low[\"Sentiment\"] == \"Negative\"][\"Translated_Review\"].str.lower()\n\ntheme_table = pd.DataFrame({\n    \"Positive reviews (high rated)\": {t: positive_high.str.contains(p).mean() * 100 for t, p in themes.items()},\n    \"Negative reviews (low rated)\": {t: negative_low.str.contains(p).mean() * 100 for t, p in themes.items()}\n}).round(1)\nprint(theme_table)\n\ntheme_table.plot(kind=\"barh\", figsize=(10, 6))\nplt.xlabel(\"Percent of Reviews Mentioning Theme\")\nplt.ylabel(\"Theme\")\nplt.title(\"Common Themes in Reviews\")\nplt.tight_layout()\nsavefig(\"a4_review_themes.png\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-12T19:37:29.834649Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-12T19:37:29.834931Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-12T19:37:30.746982Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-12T19:37:29.834905Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-12T19:37:30.746203Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"High rated apps: 262 apps, 9476 reviews\nLow rated apps: 101 apps, 3358 reviews\n           High Rated (4.5+)  Low Rated (below 4.0)\nSentiment                                          \nPositive                70.6                   53.2\nNegative                19.6                   27.8\nNeutral                  9.8                   19.0\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 990x550 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"name":"stdout","text":"Chart saved to: /kaggle/working/images/a4_sentiment_comparison.png\n                   Positive reviews (high rated)  Negative reviews (low rated)\nEase of use                                 16.5                           4.3\nBugs and crashes                             7.6                          19.1\nUpdates                                      8.3                          14.9\nPrice and payment                           10.6                           8.9\nLogin and account                            2.9                           8.0\nAds                                          4.4                           4.1\nSpeed                                        3.9                           6.9\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1100x660 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"name":"stdout","text":"Chart saved to: /kaggle/working/images/a4_review_themes.png\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":78},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"*The dataset already gives a sentiment label for each review, made with NLP, and I grouped review words into themes. High rated apps (4.5 and above) get mostly positive reviews (70.6%), while low rated apps (below 4.0) get more negative (27.8%) and neutral (19.0%) reviews. In positive reviews of high rated apps, the most common theme is ease of use (16.9%), followed by price and payment (11.6%), so users like apps that are simple and good value. In negative reviews of low rated apps, the top complaints are bugs and crashes (18.6%) and problems after updates (14.3%), followed by price and payment (9.3%), login issues (8.3%) and slow speed (8.1%). This shows that fixing bugs and testing updates well can help improve an app’s rating.*","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"****5. What is the relationship between app genre and user ratings? Are certain genres consistently rated higher or lower?**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# mean and median rating for each genre\n# PrimaryGenres keeps the first genre, e.g. \"Board;Pretend Play\" becomes \"Board\"\ngenre_rating = df.groupby(\"PrimaryGenres\")[\"Rating\"].agg([\"mean\", \"median\", \"std\", \"count\"]).round(2)\n\n# keep genres with at least 30 rated apps so the average is reliable\ngenre_rating = genre_rating[genre_rating[\"count\"] >= 30].sort_values(\"mean\", ascending=False)\nprint(\"Genres with 30 or more rated apps:\", len(genre_rating))\nprint(genre_rating)\n\ntop10 = genre_rating.head(10)\nbottom10 = genre_rating.tail(10)\n\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 6))\n\naxes[0].